{
  "request": {
    "model": "nomic-embed-text:latest",
    "input": [
      "Synthetic nurse note for software testing. No real patient data.\n\nThe nurse reviews a commercial driver's symptoms alongside information from a witness, the treating team and an older workplace form, because each source describes a different part of the story; the occupational record retains those differences and identifies completed current findings without turning a booking, a family account or a recollection into a measured patient result.\n\nThe current ophthalmologist's signed examination confirms non-physiological diplopia within 18 degrees of central fixation, reproduced during the assessment even though the driver says the two overlapping road-sign images sometimes merge after blinking; an older note reported comfortable reading at a desk, but that earlier description neither contradicts the current reproduced double vision nor establishes that a patch or new lenses have resolved it.\n\nThe usual work involves coupling trailers, checking mirrors, interpreting radio messages and responding to pedestrians in a loading area, with breaks that can be delayed when deliveries run late; the driver explains which difficulty occurred while stationary and which was noticed during ordinary duties, rather than claiming that quiet conversation in the clinic reproduces every task in the cab.\n\nThe nurse keeps the relevant current attachment with the record and identifies the older account by its timing, so a later reviewer can distinguish what was observed, what the driver reported and what remains unresolved; no additional measurement, specialist conclusion or diagnosis is added merely because it would make the occupational decision easier to complete.\n"
    ],
    "truncate": false
  },
  "provider_called": true,
  "status": "completed",
